    <string name="help_success_status_code">
        <![CDATA[
        Successful HTTP status codes. Unlisted codes are treated as failures and will stop the workflow. <br>
        <br>
        Multiple codes or ranges can be comma separated. <br>
        E.g.: <sample><b>200-299, 404</b></sample> <br>
        <br>
        <sample><b>Use case</b></sample> <br>
        &ensp; Some sites return <error>404</error> when a queried number isn\'t found, which means it\'s clean.
         A <warn><b>!</b></warn> in the history record indicates that the request failed, add <error>404</error> here to avoid that.
        ]]>
    </string>
